+# FR005 — full-CI contract and test-lane repair · 2026-10-06
+
+Base: `2e728fe4c258a963d852f8e7f3b25446ce932076`, PR47, branch `candidate/tili-task-dependencies-20261006`.
+PR45 is the unchanged base `5b88c326`; main remains outside this delivery. No merge, auto-merge or deployment.
+
+## Observed failure
+
+CI run37454159948 reported 3310 passing and 3 failing tests, zero pending/todo. The downloaded backend-diagnostics artifact11409716962 has SHA-256 `bfc3a0a5fd90c6555b61a215836daa55de9bd1c68c316df0b54e88dae02797ee`.
+
+- audit53 requires taskDependencies.test.ts in the serial group: its real lock-wait witnesses query the database-wide pg_stat_activity/pg_blocking_pids graph.
+- audit55 still expected contract0.70.0 although FR005 intentionally publishes0.71.0.
+- audit55 found four emitted 409 codes absent from OpenAPI: task_dependencies_changed, task_dependencies_pending, task_dependency_cycle and task_dependency_completed.
+
+These three exact failures reproduced locally: 27PASS/3FAIL/3SKIP. The three skipped cases require PostgreSQL and are not called passed. This explains the full-suite failure, not the outcome of migration/native steps skipped after it.
+
+## Repair
+
+Register the unchanged dependencies suite in vitest.serial.json. Keep audit53 and its shared-state detection unchanged. The existing projects select the suite once, now after parallel suites; its real concurrent requests and lock witnesses remain intact.
+
+Update the exact audit55 version assertion to0.71.0, not a loose version range. Name all four dependency conflicts in the task PATCH409 response and task_dependency_in_use in DELETE409 alongside system_task. Add five parameterized checks requiring each code in its own operation's409 response, not merely somewhere in the document.
+
+Run the repository generators for paths, schemas and both API type files. Runtime path/schema output is byte-identical; the two generated type files change documentation comments only. No application behavior, migration, access rule, dependency limit or completion guard is weakened.
+
+## Local verification before publication
+
+With all five new response-code checks present and before the repair: 27PASS/8FAIL/3SKIP. After the repair, the same expanded audits plus the existing four contract-sync checks: 39PASS/0FAIL/3SKIP. Full backend TypeScript and full backend ESLint pass. The first combined validation command hit the environment's execution timeout; successful separate commands, not the interrupted command, provide the recorded results.
+
+The source archive restores Git tree `6f6a767864a61aea333dcfc58cdecd448891d6a8` exactly. This is the real feature tree, not the earlier PR45 source. Locked backend dependencies were restored from an isolated Actions snapshot. No credentials or raw authentication fixtures are exported as evidence.
+
+Full PostgreSQL/Redis CI, schema83→84 preserving rehearsal, C04/C05 and the browser suites still require a completed run on the new published HEAD. Local static success does not stand in for those checks. Final remote results are recorded in PR47 after actual completion; no success is predeclared here.
